# Workspace .gitignore — written by `/sync init` into $JOBISSIMO_HOME.
# The workspace is your OWN private git repo. Everything here is committed and
# synced EXCEPT the few runtime/machine-specific artefacts below.

# The database is a runtime artefact, rebuilt from state/backup/*.csv by
# `db.py import-csv`. Never commit the binary DB — it changes every run and
# cannot be merged; the CSVs are the record of record.
state/*.db
state/*.db-journal
state/*.db-wal
state/*.db-shm
state/*.db.bak.*

# Machine-specific: capabilities are re-detected per machine by /doctor
# (the laptop has a browser adapter, the server may not).
config/capabilities.yaml
config/local/

# Transient
runs/.hunt_lock/
.DS_Store

# Everything else IS committed — including the exported .docx/.pdf in
# applications/. Each is written once and never modified, so git stores them
# efficiently, and for a submitted application the exact file sent is worth
# keeping. To slim the repo you may ignore artefacts for jobs that never
# reached `applied` — export.py regenerates them from the committed *_final.md.
